  "query_preview": "..\nIsland effect showers thunderstorms are the main forecast concern \nfor Guam over the next couple of days, with light and variable winds \nexpected for at least the first half of the week. Otherwise, \nisolated light showers will be the rule through Monday as the \noverall dry pattern continues. For the CNMI, expect increasing \nconvection Monday night as a weak disturbance passes by to the east \nof the islands, coming close enough to the CNMI to bring low-end \nscattered showers and possible thunderstorms. This convection will \nspread into Guam Tuesday night. This round of showers will be \nrelatively short- lived, with a dry pattern returning to the region \nWednesday morning. The dry pattern will then continue through next \nweekend.",
